09f6169a82</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:00:00 -0000</pubDate><category>untagged</category><description>arXiv cs.CR: arXiv:2611.25470v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: Large language models (LLMs) are increasingly deployed as agents that translate user requests into sequences of local tool invocations. While prior cache-based side-channel attacks target the locally deployed models, they typically require the adversary to share model-related components or hardware resources with the victim's inference process. These</description></item><item><title>Tether: Verified Stateful Policy Engine for System-Level Monitoring of Agents</title><link>https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.25599</link><guid isPermaLink="false">fe231af6f51d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:00:00 -0000</pubDate><category>untagged</category><description>arXiv cs.CR: arXiv:2611.25599v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: Autonomous AI agents are increasingly deployed for long-running tasks that execute arbitrary shell commands or programs. However, these actions can result in unauthorized network requests or persistent, malicious changes to the user's file system, processes, or privileges. Existing defense mechanisms rely on either LLM-based monitors, which lack prov</description></item><item><title>Hardening JavaScript Programs against LLM-Based Vulnerability Detection</title><link>https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.25718</link><guid isPermaLink="false">1c1c0d05263f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:00:00 -0000</pubDate><category>untagged</category><description>arXiv cs.CR: arXiv:2611.25718v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: JavaScript programs are often distributed as source code, so attackers can analyze them for vulnerabilities. LLM-based vulnerability detection agents now make this analysis much easier. To mitigate this emerging threat, we present AntiAgent, a defense that lets developers harden their programs against such detection agents. AntiAgent transforms a pro</description></item></channel></rss>